{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC1 IS MET — the pass-level assertion finally EXECUTED, and it passed. Run 30867072561.\n\nI refused to tick this from the capability map, because the map answered the PLATFORM question (the Epic Link write persists) while AC1 asks for a **pass-level** assertion that a syncable parent/child relationship actually reaches DC through a reconcile pass. That distinction is the whole discipline of this epic. It is now discharged properly.\n\n`test_outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link` **executes and passes** on run 30867072561 (`collected=58 executed=57 skipped=1`, 5 failed / 52 passed / 1 xfailed). It is absent from the failure list, and `offers no 'Epic' issue type` — its verdict on every prior run — appears nowhere in the output.\n\nIt took clearing three separate blockers to get here, each of which masked the next: the disjoint emit/apply gates (fixed by 1311's Epic Link route, after 1302's greenhopper route was refuted live), then the missing Epic issue type ([rebar:3fe5-c22e-dc2d-4c9e], change 1332), and the transport hitting the module-size cap in between ([rebar:465d-c541-5e52-4e62], change 1331, now merged).\n\n**Change 1311's mechanism is now proven at the level that matters** — not by a green unit suite, and not by a raw-REST probe, but by a reconcile pass writing a parent that a subsequent read sees. That is the standard 1276, 1288 and 1302 each failed to meet while being mutation-proven and wrong.\n\nAll five AC boxes are now satisfied. The remaining live failures are sub-task `fields.parent` cases owned by [rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda], which AC1 does not cover — AC1 asks for AT LEAST ONE real configuration where the sets intersect, and the epic-parent path is it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785808244521926001,"uuid":"08724285-f865-4825-9cdc-aeaed4ef64dd"}